course: dictionary
lesson: 5611
title: Hybrid animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hybrid is a mix of two kinds of animal. The word liger tells you what a liger is: a baby from two very different big cats. «A liger has a lion father and a tiger mother.» So the father is a lion and the mother is a tiger.
explain: Context helps again. The text says ligers almost never happen in the wild, and that they are bred in zoos and animal parks. Why? Because lions and tigers live in different places in the wild, so they rarely meet. A word like "bred" tells you people choose the parents on purpose.
explain: Look for clues about size too. The text says ligers grow bigger than both parents. Bigger than both means the baby is bigger than a lion and bigger than a tiger, so you can picture a very large cat.
fact: A liger is the baby of a male lion and a female tiger.
fact: A liger is a hybrid, which means a mix of two kinds of animal.
fact: Ligers are often bigger than both of their parents.
fact: Ligers have faint stripes and a face that looks like a lion's.
fact: Ligers almost never happen in the wild, because lions and tigers live in different places. They are mostly bred in zoos and animal parks.
exercise: What is a liger? | A kind of plant that grows in the jungle | *The baby of a male lion and a female tiger | A small striped cat that lives in the wild | A keeper who looks after big cats
exercise: Why are ligers almost never found in the wild? | Ligers only eat fish | *Lions and tigers live in different places | Ligers are too small to survive | Ligers hate the sun
exercise: In the meaning, which word means a mix of two kinds of animal? | zoo | lion | stripes | *hybrid
test: Which animal is the father of a liger? | *lion | tiger | leopard | zebra
test: «Ligers are huge.» What does huge mean? | Very small | Very quiet | *Very big | Very old
exam: Which of these is a true fact about ligers? | *They are mostly bred in zoos and animal parks | They are smaller than both parents | Their mother is always a lion | They live wild in big groups on the plains
